ull, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20407, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01VABuCmt5mBsoNaVnNEMejX", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 20407, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_0149kSWYv3dnLpBx1u4fQKhY", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 20707, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_0149kSWYv3dnLpBx1u4fQKhY", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20707, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_0149kSWYv3dnLpBx1u4fQKhY", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 25718, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_018ec2unT4KLjzVMfiMJg2VN", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc was also marked unhealthy in staging. I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback stopped partway with an orchestrator error after us-east, which left the regions on mixed versions (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). A second rollback finished in all regions. Current state: all three regions are on v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, find out why v2.3.1 was promoted when the staging RC was unhealthy, and investigate the orchestrator error that stopped the rollout.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 56318, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_018ec2unT4KLjzVMfiMJg2VN", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56318, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_018ec2unT4KLjzVMfiMJg2VN", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 57930, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01GLKutHDkmWcX7eUZoHCFQf", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 58230, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01GLKutHDkmWcX7eUZoHCFQf", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 58230, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01GLKutHDkmWcX7eUZoHCFQf", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 65521, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's passing health checks again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n- **Problem:** v2.3.1 was live in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with about 18% of requests erroring. Its test version (v2.3.1-rc) had also failed health checks in staging.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback stopped after us-east because the deployment system returned an error, which left the other two regions on v2.3.1. I ran it again and it finished in all regions.\n- **Now:** all three regions are on v2.3.0, healthy, with about 0.2% of requests erroring. No approval was needed, since v2.3.0 had been healthy in production before.\n- **Incident:** the request to open it timed out. I checked the incident list before trying again and found it had been created, so there's only one. Opening it paged the on-call engineer. It describes what happened, the rollback (including the partial failure) and three things to follow up:\n  - why v2.3.1 failed\n  - why it was released when its staging version was unhealthy\n  - what caused the deployment system error", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_018fL4L4eHFLB5hhkLuU5gdy", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01S9JCWNqm8qho3QhQMnuy6p", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01EZQ8CkHgKkof3FgaUfpLSa", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01TbdQMBkNfo5FiceF66AtVv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Only us-east got rolled back. Rolling back to the same version again should be safe to repeat, so I'll try once more.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01YZQBw5B4s11DnWxbFYB6cn", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01VABuCmt5mBsoNaVnNEMejX", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_0149kSWYv3dnLpBx1u4fQKhY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_018ec2unT4KLjzVMfiMJg2VN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc was also marked unhealthy in staging. I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback stopped partway with an orchestrator error after us-east, which left the regions on mixed versions (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). A second rollback finished in all regions. Current state: all three regions are on v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, find out why v2.3.1 was promoted when the staging RC was unhealthy, and investigate the orchestrator error that stopped the rollout.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01GLKutHDkmWcX7eUZoHCFQf", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's passing health checks again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n- **Problem:** v2.3.1 was live in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with about 18% of requests erroring. Its test version (v2.3.1-rc) had also failed health checks in staging.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback stopped after us-east because the deployment system returned an error, which left the other two regions on v2.3.1. I ran it again and it finished in all regions.\n- **Now:** all three regions are on v2.3.0, healthy, with about 0.2% of requests erroring. No approval was needed, since v2.3.0 had been healthy in production before.\n- **Incident:** the request to open it timed out. I checked the incident list before trying again and found it had been created, so there's only one. Opening it paged the on-call engineer. It describes what happened, the rollback (including the partial failure) and three things to follow up:\n  - why v2.3.1 failed\n  - why it was released when its staging version was unhealthy\n  - what caused the deployment system error", "type": "text"}]}]}